data/raw/

# Ignore all CSVs except those the application imports with `?raw`.
#
# Vite resolves a `?raw` import at build time, so an untracked file is not a missing asset at
# runtime — it is a build failure. Two CSVs are imported that way: the canonical panel and the
# observed-vs-predicted export. The second was ignored by this rule and absent from CI, where
# `Failed to resolve import` broke the build while every local check passed, because the file
# existed on the developer machine.
*.csv
!public/data/panel_canonical_v2.csv
!src/data/analysis/observed_vs_predicted_authoritative.csv

# Generated reports & debug outputs
eslint-out.txt
eslint-report.json
zip_debug.txt
zip_done.txt

# Zips & archives
*.zip
q1_share.zip

# OS-specific
Thumbs.db
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride

